---
// Experiment 1-1 context ablation matrix: which component each group removes, and what happens (redraw of Fig 1-3).
---

<svg
	class="dg"
	viewBox="0 0 720 404"
	role="img"
	aria-labelledby="d-abl-title d-abl-desc"
	style="min-width: 630px"
>
	<title id="d-abl-title">Experiment 1-1: context ablation study</title>
	<desc id="d-abl-desc">
		A matrix of five experimental groups against five context columns. System prompt and tool definitions form the
		static prefix; tool results, reasoning (assistant) and history messages form the dynamic history. The full baseline
		keeps every component and works. Removing tool definitions means the agent can't act and fabricates an answer.
		Removing tool results leaves it in a blind retry loop. Removing reasoning costs little if the reasoning can be
		reconstructed. Removing history makes it repeat operations. The system prompt is kept in every group.
	</desc>

	<text x="2" y="28" class="dg-title">Experiment 1-1: context ablation study</text>

	<g class="dg-edge">
		<path d="M100,70 V62 H281 V70"></path>
	</g>
	<text x="190" y="52" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-edge-label">static prefix</text>
	<g class="dg-edge">
		<path d="M290,70 V62 H568 V70"></path>
	</g>
	<text x="429" y="52" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-edge-label">dynamic history</text>

	<!-- Header row -->
	<g class="dg-node dg-context">
		<rect x="98" y="74" width="92" height="52" rx="6"></rect>
		<text x="144" y="95" text-anchor="middle">System</text>
		<text x="144" y="117" text-anchor="middle">prompt</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-context">
		<rect x="193" y="74" width="92" height="52" rx="6"></rect>
		<text x="239" y="95" text-anchor="middle">Tool</text>
		<text x="239" y="117" text-anchor="middle">definitions</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-harness">
